{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Curtains.</b> Made like the curtains of a ship — hole after hole, the work of braiding and not the work of weaving. And the Targum renders סְרָדִין, as the Targum of מִכְבָּר, which is rendered סְרָדָה — because they are pierced like a sieve." "<b>For the one side.</b> An entire direction is called פֵּאָה."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:56.614336677Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}